Subject:    arg: ask spec_types_is_default() about DRAFT types only, so an ngram
            method no longer suppresses draft-sidecar discovery
Upstream:   NOT FILED, and not going to be. Standing project ruling on outward
            submissions ("Someone else might refile, but not us."). There is no
            issue number to track and nobody is chasing this.
Applies to: TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant @ fb2cc35ab3507a5aab56fe593620cd96d8f45384
            (common/arg.cpp, function spec_types_is_default)

WHAT IT FIXES
=============
`spec_types_is_default()` is an EXACT vector equality against the pristine
one-element `{COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_NONE}`, and it has exactly two callers at
this pin, both inside `common_models_handler_init` / the models handler:

  * DRAFT-REPO SIDECAR DISCOVERY — when a draft repo is set with `-hfd` and no
    type was requested, ask the repo for every sidecar it ships (mtp, dflash,
    eagle3, dspark) so the type can be inferred afterwards.
  * SIDECAR TYPE INFERENCE — pick the speculative type from whichever sidecar the
    draft repo actually produced (mtp > dspark > dflash > eagle3).

Both are asking the same real question: HAS THE USER ALREADY CHOSEN A DRAFT TYPE?
Exact equality answers a different and stricter one: is the type vector untouched?

⇒ ANY value in that vector suppresses both, INCLUDING THE NGRAM METHODS, which
have nothing to do with a draft repo. The ngram types
(`NGRAM_SIMPLE`, `NGRAM_MAP_K`, `NGRAM_MAP_K4V`, `NGRAM_MOD`, `NGRAM_CACHE`) are
model-free — they draft from the context that is already there, and they say
NOTHING about which sidecar a draft repository should contribute. Selecting one
should leave draft discovery entirely alone.

The concrete failure this produces here: `--spec-default` PUSHES `NGRAM_MOD` onto
`params.speculative.types`, so with it on, `-hfd <repo>` alone never fetches the
repo's sidecar and never infers DFlash/MTP/Eagle3/DSpark. The user gets a plain
full-model draft (or nothing) and is told nothing about it. Every symptom is a
non-event: the image builds, the server starts, /health answers 200, and a
feature the user asked for by naming a draft repo simply did not happen.

⇒ THIS PATCH REPLACES THE EQUALITY WITH `std::none_of` OVER THE SIX `DRAFT_*`
TYPES. The predicate now means what its callers need it to mean, and ngram and an
auto-discovered draft sidecar can be used together.

THE SIX ARE ENUMERATED FROM THE ENUM, NOT FROM MEMORY
=====================================================
`enum common_speculative_type` in common/common.h, at this pin, spells the draft
family as: `DRAFT_SIMPLE`, `DRAFT_EAGLE3`, `DRAFT_MTP`, `DRAFT_MTP_ADAPTIVE`,
`DRAFT_DFLASH`, `DRAFT_DSPARK`. Everything else in the enum is `NONE`, one of the
five `NGRAM_*` values, or the `COUNT` sentinel.

⚠️ A NEW DRAFT TYPE ADDED UPSTREAM IS NOT VISIBLE TO THIS PATCH. It would apply
cleanly and silently under-report, exactly as the pre-patch code over-reported.
Re-read the enum at every pin bump; the guard cannot see this for you, because a
name that does not exist yet cannot be counted.

`<algorithm>` IS ALREADY INCLUDED
=================================
Verified at this pin, not assumed: common/arg.cpp includes `<algorithm>` in its
own include block, and the file already uses `std::find` in
`common_models_handler_init` immediately below this function. No new include, no
new API, no other file touched.

WHAT WOULD MAKE IT REMOVABLE (a condition to NOTICE, not an outcome to expect)
=============================================================================
🚨 THIS IS NOT A PATCH WE EXPECT TO CARRY FOREVER, AND THE GUARD SAYS SO IN TWO
DIRECTIONS. The bug is in ggml-org's own tree, it affects their own feature
combination (ngram drafting plus a draft repo), and it can be fixed without us —
so "they might fix it" is a live possibility here rather than a theoretical one.
The anchor guard in scaffolding/Container.llama-build distinguishes the two
outcomes, and they call for opposite actions:

  * the stock equality predicate is GONE and our replacement is absent ⇒ READ the
    function at the new ref. If upstream now excludes the ngram types itself,
    DELETE this file and the guard. Do not re-derive a hunk for a fix that is
    already there.
  * the stock predicate is still present but the hunk fails at fuzz 0 ⇒ ordinary
    drift. RE-DERIVE the hunk at the new sha and update the guard's counts to
    match what you actually found.

⚠️ AND IT CAN STOP MATTERING WITHOUT FAILING TO APPLY. If nothing calls
`spec_types_is_default()` any more, this patch applies perfectly and changes
nothing. That is why the guard also asserts the function is still CALLED.

⚠️ THAT CALL-SITE ASSERTION IS A FLOOR (`-ge 2`), DELIBERATELY. ggml-org master
already carries a THIRD call site (type inference from the draft GGUF's metadata)
that our pin does not have, so pinning the count exactly would go red on a rebase
that changes nothing this patch depends on. The floor still catches the failure
that matters, which is nobody calling it at all.

VERIFIED 2026-09-07 against ggml-org/llama.cpp master: the stock exact-equality
predicate is still there, unchanged, and its call sites number THREE (draft-repo
sidecar discovery, sidecar type inference, and the GGUF-metadata inference above).
So upstream has not fixed this, and the floor is measured rather than guessed.

THE BLANK CONTEXT LINES ARE A SINGLE SPACE — DO NOT LET AN EDITOR STRIP THEM
===========================================================================
The hunk's leading and trailing context both include an empty source line, and a
canonical unified diff spells one as a single space. Tools that trim trailing
whitespace turn them into truly empty lines, which makes GNU patch apply this
with fuzz — and the guard runs `patch -F0`, so it would then fail outright. That
is the strictness working as intended; the fix is to restore the spaces, never to
relax the fuzz.

--- a/common/arg.cpp
+++ b/common/arg.cpp
@@ -360,7 +360,20 @@
 }
 
 static bool spec_types_is_default(const common_params & params) {
-    return params.speculative.types == std::vector<enum common_speculative_type>{COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_NONE};
+    // "default" here means "no draft type has been chosen", because the only thing the
+    // callers do with the answer is decide whether to discover/infer a draft sidecar.
+    // The ngram methods are model-free -- they draft from the context itself and say
+    // nothing about which sidecar a draft repo should contribute -- so their presence
+    // must not suppress that discovery. Ask for the absence of the DRAFT_* types only.
+    return std::none_of(params.speculative.types.begin(), params.speculative.types.end(),
+        [](enum common_speculative_type type) {
+            return type == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_SIMPLE
+                || type == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_EAGLE3
+                || type == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_MTP
+                || type == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_MTP_ADAPTIVE
+                || type == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_DFLASH
+                || type == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_DSPARK;
+        });
 }
 
